\title{Statement on LLMs}
\author{brentyorgey}
\date{2026-03-07T21:55:40Z}

\p{I do not and will not use LLMs, in any form, for any purpose.  Although LLMs are fascinating from a purely technical perspective, I refuse to participate in or contribute to such systems that are built on massive exploitation of human labor and make profligate use of scarce resources.  I also don't think they are actually very good for a lot of the applications people seem excited about.  Even in cases where LLMs are technically good at a task, that does not necessarily mean their use for that task contributes positively to human flourishing.}

\p{A good way to describe myself is as a [generative AI vegetarian](https://sboots.ca/2026/03/11/generative-ai-vegetarianism/).  You can find a fuller explanation—and many, many links—at the above essay by Sean Boots, which I agree with almost 100\%.}
